  <bioghist id="0a489e6974bf9f68568cd8c44313de13">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>Judith Samuelson joined the Ford Foundation in 1989 as Director of the Office of Program-Related Investments. In 1994 she helped launch the Foundation's Corporate Involvement Initiative, a program to substantially increase the involvement of corporations in community and economic development (CED). Samuelson left the Foundation in 1996 and became Executive Director of the Business and Society Program at the Aspen Institute in 1998.</p>  </bioghist>
